        "findings": [
          "General complex categorifiability remains unresolved. The pointed subcategory must be untwisted Vec(C5), the regular-algebra Morita dual must have the same fusion ring, and no braided categorification exists. These restrictions provide neither a model nor a general exclusion.",
          "The pointed-associator theorem rules out every nonzero H³(C5,C×) class.",
          "Based-ring equality of the Morita dual does not imply a tensor equivalence or a central lift.",
          "The necessary twist orders divide 1600. Surviving integer Gram data are not categorical models."
        ]
      }
